    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green). \n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence:\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds the code from three parts:\n- `CITY3`: upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- `LAST3`: upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN`: 4-digit zero-padded sequence = one more than the owners *already in that city* (counted via `findAll().stream().filter(city match)`, run before save so only existing owners count), replacing the previous global count.\n\n**Derived values rebuilt:** `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` already builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` by reading `getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically picks up the new format (e.g. `TOW-SMI-0007-M26`). No other code derives from `customerCode`.\n\n**Docs updated** for accuracy: the javadoc on both function classes and the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` descriptions and examples in `openapi.yml`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (which asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, as does the full suite.",
